<title>USA: Datastrip says court dismisses Symbol Tech claim.</title>
<headline>Datastrip says court dismisses Symbol Tech claim.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Datastrip Ltd said on Friday that the U.S. District Court of Delaware had dismissed counterlcaims made against the company by Symbol Technologies Inc.</p>
<p>The counterclaims held that Datastrip's patented two-dimensional bar code was fraudulently procured, Datastrip said in a statement, and that Datastrip misused its patent.</p>
<p>The claim responded to a suit brought against Symbol Tech by Datastrip in February for patent infringement.</p>
<p>Datastrip, based in the Isle of Man, designs optical scanners that read printed bar codes.</p>
</text>
